error_signature: "ld.lld: error: duplicate symbol: rle_auxtab"
root_cause: "A header file declares a non-static const array as a tentative definition (`const uint8_t rle_auxtab[8];` in rle.h). Every translation unit that includes the header emits its own common symbol; with modern Clang's default -fno-common the linker sees multiple strong definitions and fails with `duplicate symbol`. In fermi-lite 0.1 the symbols collide when linking fml-asm (misc.o/rope.o/rle.o all include rle.h)."
rec_approach: "Change the header to a pure declaration (`extern const uint8_t rle_auxtab[8];`) and keep the single definition in exactly one .c file (rle.c). No ABI or behavior change; the object layout stays identical."
match_keywords: ["duplicate symbol", "rle_auxtab", "tentative definition", "extern declaration", "-fno-common", "header global", "link error"]
error_excerpt: "ld.lld: error: duplicate symbol: rle_auxtab / >>> defined at rle.h:33 (./rle.h:33) / >>>            misc.o:(rle_auxtab) in archive libfml.a"
severity: P1
category: headers, linking, c
last_updated: 2026-09-26